Chapter: E1000SwflagStrict
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci

Section: Fixtures

  bring-up : PciScanResult -> E1000Device
  bring-up (scan) =
    when e1000-find scan
      is Just (d) -> e1000-init d
      is None -> e1000-absent

Section: Judges

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

Section: Entry

 THE ARM FOR THE REQUEST CARRYING ONLY OUR OWN BIT. 82583V 4.5.2 gives each
 agent one ownership bit and says at most one is 1b at any time, so a write
 that asserts MNG or HW registers a request on another agent's behalf. Until
 2026-08-24 `e1000-swflag-acquire` read-modify-wrote the whole register and did
 exactly that whenever firmware held MNG, which is what the board reads
 (`extcnf 0x00F00=002c0089`).

 NO ARM COULD SEE IT, AND THAT IS WHY THIS ONE EXISTS. The bed preserved
 firmware's MNG whatever software wrote, so the violation had no consequence
 and a read-modify-writing driver was indistinguishable from a correct one:
 `e1000-swflag`, `e1000-swflag-mng`, `e1000-swflag-refused` and
 `e1000-swflag-k1` all pass with the defect present. `-i219-extcnf-strict`
 models a part that enforces the rule instead of tolerating it: a foreign
 assertion latches, and while latched SW ownership is never granted.

 SO THIS ARM IS FALSIFIABLE BY CONSTRUCTION. The acquire must answer 1 and the
 flag must be held. A driver that asserts a bit it does not own cannot reach
 either, and the pre-fix driver was measured doing so 6,002 times in this same
 configuration. `violated` staying clear is the whole claim.

 THE FLAG IS NOT A STATEMENT ABOUT THE PART. Whether the real PCH enforces
 4.5.2 is uncited and is the campaign's open proposition; 4.5.2 itself says the
 mechanism does not block software accesses. This arm measures the DRIVER
 against the protocol, which is ours to get right either way.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let scan = pci-scan-bus 0
    in let d = bring-up scan
    in let mmio = d.e-mmio
    in let got = e1000-swflag-acquire mmio e1000-swflag-fuel
    in let held = e1000-swflag-held mmio
    in let ext = e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-extcnf-ctrl
    in act
      print-line-uni ("acquire answers    : " & show got)
      print-line-uni ("flag held          : " & yn held)
      print-line-uni ("mng asserted by us : " & yn (bit-and ext e1000-extcnf-mng-own /= 0))
      print-line-uni ("released clean     : " & show (e1000-swflag-release mmio))
    end
  end

